I think fence does need to be in there in order to be my unit of replication. Each block has two fences in it and WW is applied at each fence. So fence is nested within block and WW is the split plot factor at each fence. This gives me n=6 for testing WW effects, but gives me n=12 for SW and WW*SW effects because each level of SW is applied to two sub-plots at each of the 6 fences. Without fence in the model I think it treats block as the unit of replication for WW and fence as the unit of replication for SW, averaging the replicate sub-plots at each fence.
