D-RUG,

I have a coding issue I'm struggling with that hopefully there's a simple solution to. I am trying to make a time series plot of chlorophyll-a concentration over time from measurements taken by a buoy offshore of the Bodega Marine Lab.

Here's my code:

d = read.csv("Oceanographic data BML buoy 2014.csv")
newdata = d[6141:11574, ] #  subsets data for the dates I'm interested in

times = strptime(newdata$INSTRUMENT_DATETIME, format="%m/%d/%y  %H:%M") #strips data and gives it formatting for POSIX format
times = as.POSIXct(times) #makes R know its a date/time

plot(times,newdata$CHLOROPHYLL,
     type="l", ylab="Chlorophyll a (μg/L)", xlab="", xaxt="n")
times2=format(times, "%m/%d") # running just this line shows that it works in that it removes the year from the date
times2<-as.POSIXct(times2, format="%m/%d") #this seems to be where it breaks down and reinserts the year into the date
S=seq(as.POSIXct(times2[1]),as.POSIXct(times2[length(times2)]), by="3 days")
axis.POSIXct(1,times2,at=S,label=S,format="%m/%d", las=2)

I received some of this code from a postdoc in my lab, so I do not fully understand this whole POSIX.ct coding. In fact, I find it rather counterintuitive, which seems to be a reoccurring theme when it comes to my thoughts on R code. I've attached the data file if anyone actually wants to run the data and/or make the plot themselves.

Any help or thoughts would be much appreciated!
Matt

